PSF tensor provenance
---------------------
The two files in summicron/_artifacts/ are tables of point spread functions
ray-traced with optiland (PyPI package `optiland`, MIT licence).

* psf_lens35_us3006249_fu0.4.npz is traced from the prescription in
  US 3,006,249, Example II (a United States patent; inventor W. Mandler,
  assignee Ernst Leitz Canada; filed 1958; expired, public domain), scaled to
  a 35 mm focal length at f/2.
* psf_lens50_doublegauss_fu0.4.npz is traced from the 50 mm f/2 double-Gauss
  sample prescription that ships with optiland.

optiland is Copyright (c) 2024 Kramer Harrison and is distributed under the
MIT License. The 50 mm sample prescription is taken from optiland and remains
under that licence; the tensor built from it is distributed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0 together with the rest of this repository.

These are ray-traced design prescriptions, not measurements of any production
lens. The build is reproducible with scripts/build_psf/ and
environment-optiland.yml.

Third-party model weights
-------------------------
The optional monocular depth fallback uses Depth Anything V2 Small
(Apache-2.0). Its weights are downloaded from Hugging Face at first use and are
not redistributed in this repository or in the wheel.

